#!/bin/sh
# Refuses a push to main. Every change reaches main through a pull request (README, "How we review").
# GitHub cannot lock main on this free private repo, so this hook is the lock on each laptop.
# make setup and make hooks turn it on.
while read -r local_ref local_sha remote_ref remote_sha; do
  if [ "$remote_ref" = "refs/heads/main" ]; then
    cat >&2 <<'MSG'

Push refused: main only changes through a pull request. Nothing was pushed, and your commits are safe.

Move your commits to a branch, then push the branch:

  git switch -c feat/my-change        # a new branch that keeps your commits
  git branch -f main origin/main      # put your main back to match GitHub
  git push -u origin feat/my-change

Then open a pull request on GitHub. CONTRIBUTING.md has every step.

MSG
    exit 1
  fi
done
exit 0
